QIK-VRT UNIVERSAL TRANSPUTER — C90 TARGET ENTRYPOINT

Human architecture and direction: Ingolf Lohmann.
Implementation and verification in this work unit: OpenAI Codex.
Work unit: state/work_units/UNIVERSAL_TRANSPUTER_C90_BUS_20260921_V1.json
Branch: architecture/universal-transputer-c90-v1

Read next/README.md and next/TARGET_ENTRYPOINTS.json, then resolve the actual
HEAD and TREE of this checkout. A branch name or chat summary is not a version.

The universal Transputer is present at:
  next/core/include/qikvrt_transputer.h
  next/core/include/qikvrt_bus.h
  next/core/src/qikvrt_exchange.c
  next/core/src/qikvrt_bus.c

It is an allocation-free C90 core for bound inter-layer messages and addressed
bus requests/responses. The existing C90 Effect Acknowledgement core remains
src/effect_ack_core.c with include/qikvrt/effect_ack.h. Its integer state codes
are explicitly translated to the unchanged QVRT v1 wire state codes.

TCP/IP is an adapter beneath the logical bus. next/crates/qikvrt/src/bus.rs
provides authenticated full-duplex IPv4/IPv6 connections, durable per-peer
outboxes and correlated EAP replies. Peers can initiate and answer concurrently.
next/crates/qikvrt/src/store.rs retains identity, originals, versions and results.

Reconstruct from persistent state; never silently initialize an absent store.
Reachability expiry and disconnects change observations, not registered identity.
Use a new directory for restore-store. Preserve original snapshots and external
checkpoints. Connection/MAC sequence numbers are not causal evidence.

Reproduction:
  make -C next/core test assembly
  cargo test --locked --manifest-path next/Cargo.toml
  cargo build --release --locked --manifest-path next/Cargo.toml
  python3 next/tools/check_bus.py
  python3 next/tools/check_exchange.py
  python3 next/tools/check_continuity.py
  python3 next/tools/check_hardware.py

Generate the current exact source catalog with:
  python3 next/tools/carrier.py catalog --head HEAD
Import it as a successor of the old registrations, retaining all original
versions. next/component-catalog.json preserves ten earlier components at
26bc470bf553f471abc02e65950acaffb3e5302a. The full six-language EAP sources from
PR #1137 are preserved with exact source bindings in next/reference/full-core-draft03/SOURCE.json.

Tests prove their declared finite domains and executed software flows. A copied
proof does not validate a successor. Physical board boot, synthesis timing,
native review, Main promotion, a release and public deployment each need their
own exact evidence. Bus admission and transport receipts do not grant ordinary
release. Keys remain in operator-owned private configuration outside Git.
